    [tpu] SWA KV pool: device/dtype-safe index mapping + fused KV buffer
    
    Make the sliding-window-attention KV pool work on TPU:
    
    - translate_loc_from_full_to_swa: move the CPU index tensor onto the
      mapping's device before indexing. On TPU kv_indices can arrive on CPU
      while full_to_swa_index_mapping lives on the TPU device, which
      otherwise raises a device-mismatch error.
    - SWA index-mapping assignments: cast indices to int64 and cast the
      assigned values to the mapping dtype unconditionally (previously only
      the NPU branch cast). TPU requires matching dtype/int64 index on the
      scatter assignment; the plain CUDA path relied on implicit casting.
    - Add get_fused_kv_buffer, delegating to the per-pool fused buffer.
      The TPU pallas RPA v3 backend reads K/V from a single fused buffer,
      so the SWA wrapper must expose it alongside get_kv_buffer.

